# SRG-APP-000068-AU-000035  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must display the Standard Mandatory DoW Notice and
# Consent Banner before granting access to the Central Log Server.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000068-AU-000035
group:           V-221905
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000048
control_rev5:    AC-8

contribution:    Splunk Web renders operator-supplied content on its login page before any
                 credential is accepted, through web.conf login_content, which is the
                 application's mechanism for presenting the Standard Mandatory Notice and
                 Consent Banner ahead of access. Note that in this release the
                 specification states the platform sanitizes the supplied HTML "by removing
                 potentially dangerous tags and attributes", so the banner must be
                 expressed in markup the sanitizer preserves rather than in the
                 script-based dialog the product STIG fix text shows.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] login_content non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] login_content matches You are accessing a U\.S\. Government \(USG\) Information System \(IS\)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] login_content https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/developing-views-and-apps-for-splunk-web/9.0/customize-splunk-web/customize-the-login-page
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The product STIG scopes this check to the instance used as a search head
                 and marks it not applicable on an instance that is not a search head, so
                 the role of the instance under review decides applicability.
external:        Access paths that do not pass through the Splunk Web login page - the
                 command line interface, the REST interface, and a single sign-on portal
                 that authenticates the user before Splunk Web is reached - present their
                 own banner or none; those are carried by the operating system logon banner
                 and by the SSO portal respectively.
external:        The exact approved banner text, including any short-form variant
                 authorized for the system, is set by the organization.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16 ([settings]), 233-237 (login_content =
                 <string>, no default, "Supports any text including HTML. The Splunk
                 platform sanitizes HTML for security purposes by removing potentially
                 dangerous tags and attributes"); product STIG SPLK-CL-000080 check and fix
                 text (add/modify the login_content line carrying the banner wording).
finding:         Splunk Web does not display the Standard Mandatory Notice and Consent
                 Banner before granting access, because web.conf [settings] login_content
                 is empty or does not carry the mandated notice text; this is assessed at
                 the application layer alone, and banners for the command line interface,
                 the REST interface, and any single sign-on portal ahead of Splunk Web are
                 recorded as external dependencies.
